change his life  that was where he met a friend of his  who happen to work at Milan's largest  department store and who would give him  his first break into the fashion  industry after the meeting Armani said  that he had become believer in destiny  that destiny has made him known for his  costly tailored sleep power suits and  clean high-quality fabrics that everyone  from the who's who of Hollywood to the  bankers on Wall Street have fallen in  love with now Jorge Armani's company has  over 1.5 billion dollars in revenue and  a retail empire that  to more than 35 countries by following  his passion and by having the courage to  switch careers Giorgio Armani was able  to go from almost poverty to building  one of the most successful businesses in  the fashion industry to help you explode  your business here are three action  items that you can learn from Giorgio  Armani action them number one stick to  your vision as an entrepreneur it's  important to have a vision that guides  your business decisions what bigger game  are you playing  what kind of mark you want to leave on  your industry what do you stand for as a  person answering these questions and  keeping your vision top of mind will  help make the difficult decisions easier  while you're in the day-to-day of  running your business for over 30 years  Armani has made a name for himself as a  designer whose clothing was elegant yet  subtle from day one he has stood out  from his competitors including the likes  of Gianni Versace who chose instead to  emphasize the sexuality of clothes over  those subtlety and has increased the  risk a nature whose designs each year  Hermione's approach to the fashion was a  pragmatic one his vision was to create  clothing that was both classic that  would send a test of time and that was  meticulously designed that was a vision  he stayed true to throughout his entire  career unlike many of his competitors  Armani believed that fashion should  evolve over time rather than change  drastically each and every year  according to our money remained true to  yourself in your philosophy  I designed for real people I think of  our customers all the time there is no  virtue whatsoever in creating clothing  or accessories that are not practical  you have to think of the future if not  we would close down I find a gratifying  that I've launched a lasting style but  of course I feel the need to reach  forward to questioner myself to take  risks I always want to refresh and renew  action limb number two stretch your  brand the easiest way to grow business  is to sell more products and services to  existing clients provided that it fits  your long-term vision and it adds more  value to your customers look for ways to  expand your business by adding new  offerings if your clients are happy with  what they've already bought from you  then they'll line up to keep working  with you  you're not just growing a business  you're finding new ways to help  customers solve problems there was never  any doubts when it came to our monies  talents of the designer however when his  partner in both life and business passed  away our money was left to defend his  talent as a businessman he had little to  no business experience but didn't want  to give up on his dream of expanding his  company to this end their money decided  to create new product lines including  many less exclusive and less expensive  spin-offs of his luxury label he  introduced Armani Jeans for casual  clothes and Armani Exchange which  consists of trending urban clothing  while he's primarily still known the  world over for his fashion designs a  mining has moved on from clothing to  launch product lines and include  accessories home furnishings restaurants  car interiors chocolates and most  recently hotels  according to Armani when I began making  jeans the press was skeptical that  someone who made luxury ready-to-wear  could start something so commercial but  I considered it a medium to speak with a  less affluent clientele  I have always paid great attention to  having brands that don't overlap I  choose a brand for a particular market  and balance my collections in terms of  look price distribution and location  when supply of fashion items become so  enormous the consumer tends to choose  the leading brand which means that  others are left behind and to establish  real credibility is no simple matter  actually um number three follow your  conscience as you grow your business  your values will be tested numerous  times do you say yes to a deal that  might make you a lot of money but isn't  in line with what you believe in when  things aren't black and white how far  are you willing to walk down the gray  line let your conscience be your guide  new opportunities will continue coming  to you you don't need to compromise who  you are to be a successful entrepreneur  our money believes at the heart of all  successful businesses are successful  relationships thus establishing positive  interactions between his company and its  communities and consumers is a  in step towards generating healthy  business growth to this end our money  has committed his company to what he  believes are positive social ideals our  money is at the forefront of companies  demonstrating the potential to be a  force for change he's refusing operating  the bubble design and luxury clothes for  consumers irrespective of the world in  which they all live much like he stood  up in the face of critics who thought he  would never make it as a businessman so  towards armani now standing up for the  social issues he believes in and proving  that any company can do the same  according to armani it is a fact that in  the West we live in a capitalist society  but that doesn't mean that we cannot be  guided by the idea of a social  conscience in our work yes fashion  design requires consumers to consume but  we can do our bit for society by running  our companies in a socially responsible  way and by creating products that  promote respect for social and  environmental issues the best way to  make a contribution fashion is to  promote the idea that a fundamental  interest in preserving the environment  is itself fashionable  so remember stick to your vision stretch  your brand and follow your conscience to  finish up this video I wanted to share  one of my favorite true stories about  George Armani and some of his most  inspirational quotes our money has  designed clothing for some of the most  influential people on the planet but  according to Monty himself some of his  proudest designs were for Princess  Charlene of Monaco  he's been clothing her since she first  wore one of his pieces in 2008 at the  Olympic Games in Beijing he spoke to  Vogue magazine about designing her  wedding gown and believes Princess  Charlene knows how to wear my creations  with nonchalance and confidence of youth  getting to the point where a royalty  requests a specific designers clothing  is considered the pinnacle of a  designer's career where our money  continues to challenge the market and  reinvent his designs which was shown in  his design for Princess Charlene's  wedding dress  according to Armani I felt the new  design was appropriate given that there  would inevitably be comparisons with  Princess Grace and those such  comparisons are of course a sign of  admiration each person has their own  individual and unique style and styles  and expression of the times he goes on  the save it was one of his greatest  creations  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  thank you for joining me for another  edition modeling the masters if you  liked the video you want to see more  please give it a thumbs up below it  makes me want to do more of these videos  for you guys I'd also love to hear what  you have to think if you want to leave a  comment under the video so thank you and  you'll see you on the next episode  [Music]  you  [Music]

